    "https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35856": {
      "title": "Early Childhood Teacher Assistant",
      "description": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities | Early Childhood Teacher Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Current UNCG Employee Log In UNC System Careers Early Childhood Teacher Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Number 998072 Functional Title Early Childhood Teacher Assistant Position Type Staff Position Eclass EZ - EHRA Non - Exempt Permanent University Information Located in North Carolina’s third largest city, UNC Greensboro is among the most diverse, learner-centered public research universities in the state, with 18,000 students in eight colleges and schools pursuing more than 150 areas of undergraduate and over 200 areas of graduate study. UNCG continues to be recognized nationally for academic excellence, access, and affordability. UNCG is ranked No. 1 most affordable institution in North Carolina for net cost by the N.Y. Times and No. 1 in North Carolina for social mobility by The Wall Street Journal — helping first-generation and lower-income students find paths to prosperity. Designated an Innovation and Economic Prosperity University by the Association of Public and Land-grant Universities, UNCG is a community-engaged research institution with a portfolio of more than $67M in research and creative activity. The University’s 2,600 staff help create an annual economic impact for the Piedmont Triad region in excess of $1B. Primary Purpose of the Organizational Unit The Child Care Education Program is operated by the Department of Human Development and Family Studies ( HDFS ), in the School of Health and Human Sciences at the University of North Carolina Greensboro. HDFS is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service regarding human development and close relationships across the lifespan. Our objectives are to educate the next generation of HDFS professionals and scholars, to generate new knowledge, and to foster the well-being of individuals and families in their everyday lives. The Child Care Education Program provides a setting where university students can gain experiential and hands-on learning, as well as have opportunities to apply content knowledge from their courses. Students are provided the opportunity to complete full-time student teaching, participate in weekly practicum placements, complete one-time observations for class assignments, and find part-time employment through work/study programs. Position Summary Early Childhood Education Teachers Assistants in the Child Care Education Program will work in a classroom as part of the consistent teaching team. They are responsible for assisting the Lead Teacher with curriculum planning in classrooms for young children, maintaining licensing and accreditation standards, creating a respectful high-quality classroom environment, caregiving routines, classroom activities, supervising groups of children indoors and outdoors, and light housekeeping duties such as serving or cleaning after meals. Minimum Qualifications An associate’s degree in early childhood; or a related field or higher and 6 months of experience working in a licensed childcare setting; or a high school diploma with 2 years of experience in a licensed childcare setting. Additional Required Certifications, Licensures, and Certificates Preferred Qualifications Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Range $32,136 - $33,100 Org #-Department Human Devlp and Family Studies - 12403 Job Open Date 09/01/2026 For Best Consideration Date Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes FTE 1.000 Type of Appointment Permanent If time-limited, please specify end date for appointment. Number of Months per Year 12 FLSA Non-Exempt Key Responsibilities ________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Percentage Of Time 20 Key Responsibility Meet or exceed licensing and accreditation standards while providing a high-quality classroom environment for young children. Essential Tasks Follow guidelines and requirements provided by NC Div. of Child Development and Early Education, as well as standards of the NAEYC Academy for Early Education. Percentage Of Time 20 Key Responsibility Assist the lead teacher in maintain up-to-date documentation on individual child assessment of growth and development for children in assigned classroom. Essential Tasks Assist the teaching by collecting anecdotal notes of each child’s progress. Become proficient in connecting this child assessment information to the developmental continuum as presented in the NC Foundations of Early Learning. Percentage Of Time 20 Key Responsibility Assist the lead teacher in planning daily curriculum using observations of children’s development and interests. Essential Tasks Participate in daily team planning time. Assist with planning curriculum activities based on observations of children. Assist with implementing the daily activities. Assist with the preparation and cleaning up of daily activities. Percentage Of Time 20 Key Responsibility Assist the leader teacher in the creating of a safe, respectful and nurturing learning environment Essential Tasks Participate in active supervision both indoors and outdoors. Assist the lead teacher in building relationships with students and families. Percentage Of Time 20 Key Responsibility Assists the teacher with caregiving routines and light housekeeping duties Essential Tasks Assist students with feeding, dressing and toileting as necessary. Assist with meal set up and clean up. Assist the teacher in the care and cleaning of learning materials both indoors and outdoors. ADA Checklist ADA Checklist R for Rare (0-30%), O for Occasional (30-60%), F for Frequent (60-90%), C for Constant (90-100%). Physical Effort Hand Movement-Repetitive Motions, Hand Movement-Grasping, Holding, Writing, Hearing, Talking, Standing, Sitting, Walking, Lifting-0-30 lbs., Lifting-30-60 lbs., Climbing-Stairs, Bending, Squatting, Crawling, Reaching, Others… - Ability to move quickly over multiple surfaces Work Environment Inside, Outside Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate how you learned of the vacant position for which you are applying: UNCGjobsearch Website Greensboro News & Record Carolina Peacemaker Other Newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education Inside Higher Ed Other Professional Journal NCWorks.gov UNC System Job Board Other Online Job Board Personal Networking Other * If you selected \"Other\", please provide the name of the resource here. (Open Ended Question) * Are you eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment at the University of North Carolina in Greensboro? Yes No UNCG Human Resources UNC Greensboro 723 Kenilworth St. Greensboro, NC 27402-6170 Telephone 336.334.5009 Fax 336.334.5585 Back to top Copyright © 2025. UNC Greensboro. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35628": {
      "title": "Academic Records Specialist",
      "description": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities | Academic Records Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Current UNCG Employee Log In UNC System Careers Academic Records Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Number 000423 Functional Title Academic Records Specialist Position Type Staff Position Eclass EZ - EHRA Non - Exempt Permanent University Information Located in North Carolina’s third largest city, UNC Greensboro is among the most diverse, learner-centered public research universities in the state, with 18,000 students in eight colleges and schools pursuing more than 150 areas of undergraduate and over 200 areas of graduate study. UNCG continues to be recognized nationally for academic excellence, access, and affordability. UNCG is ranked No. 1 most affordable institution in North Carolina for net cost by the N.Y. Times and No. 1 in North Carolina for social mobility by The Wall Street Journal — helping first-generation and lower-income students find paths to prosperity. Designated an Innovation and Economic Prosperity University by the Association of Public and Land-grant Universities, UNCG is a community-engaged research institution with a portfolio of more than $67M in research and creative activity. The University’s 2,600 staff help create an annual economic impact for the Piedmont Triad region in excess of $1B. Primary Purpose of the Organizational Unit In support of the mission of UNC Greensboro, the University Registrar’s Office fosters student success and cultivates exemplary student experiences for all University constituents related to academic records, policies, and regulations. Position Summary Reporting to the Assistant Registrar, the Academic Records Specialist is responsible for degree clearance support; tracking of degree progress, certification of graduation for undergraduate students; and serves as a point of contact for the degree clearance area. This position communicates with students, advisors, and other faculty and staff to ensure that graduation applicants have met the requirements for their degrees. This position also assists students needing notarization of documents for the purpose of obtaining an apostille and serves as a backup for ordering diplomas. Additionally, this position will collaborate with the Degree Works team to process curriculum modifications and input foreign language placement test scores and waivers for students. This position works collaboratively with Admissions and Transfer Articulation and is responsible for the daily management of the processes associated with Degree Works and graduation clearance for students. This position is responsible for maintaining current knowledge of academic courses, program requirements, and University Catalog policies at UNC Greensboro. The Academic Records Specialist works with others to implement institutional strategic initiatives and ensure compliance with statewide policies and initiatives. This position will work closely with faculty and academic affairs staff to develop proficiency in college academic requirements and to support strategic measures with the UNC System. Minimum Qualifications BACHELOR’S DEGREE ; OR EQUIVALENT COMBINATION OF TRAINING AND EXPERIENCE . ALL DEGREES MUST BE RECEIVED FROM APPROPRIATELY ACCREDITED INSTITUTIONS . Additional Required Certifications, Licensures, and Certificates Preferred Qualifications Experience in a registrar’s, admissions, or academic services environment. Experience using student information systems (Banner 9) and Degree Works. Strong commitment for innovation as demonstrated by an ability to be proactive, dynamic, forward-thinking, strategic and collaborative. Demonstrated critical thinking, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated ability to effectively communicate and foster collaboration with a wide variety of university clientele. Excellent attention to details. Excellent organizational, administrative and time management skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Suite (Word, Excel, Access, and PowerPoint) Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Range $38,000- $47,805 Org #-Department University Registrar's Office - 10204 Job Open Date 08/06/2026 For Best Consideration Date Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes FTE 1.000 Type of Appointment Permanent If time-limited, please specify end date for appointment. Number of Months per Year 12 FLSA Non-Exempt Key Responsibilities ________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Percentage Of Time 30% Key Responsibility Degree Works Curriculum Modifications Essential Tasks Process substitutions/waivers associated with student curriculum modification forms. Resolve issues through collaboration with advising team. Ensure substitutions/waivers are processed in a timely manner. Run/reconcile unhooked exception reports. Run monthly curriculum modification count report. Compile annual Course Driven Program Revision ( CDPR ) report. Assist with facilitating training workshops and creating user documentation/videos. Document/maintain internal process documentation related to functional responsibilities. Establish/maintain communication with user community. Percentage Of Time 60% Key Responsibility Degree Clearance Support Essential Tasks Track degree progress and certify graduation for undergraduate students. Track and certify awarding of pre-baccalaureate certificates. Evaluate degree audit, assess missing requirements, and provide solutions to resolve outstanding issues. Respond to emails via the generic email account. Provide knowledgeable support through the degree clearance/pre-bacc awarding process to make expectations and requirements easily understandable. Navigate each individual student situation by applying a complex set of academic policies and procedures, while maintaining a seamless student experience. Provide expertise and support to students, faculty, and staff to resolve outstanding issues and make decisions around applying program rules in non-standard situations. Maintain current knowledge of Banner system technical releases and implications of releases on business processes and assist with Banner testing. Assist with training/mentoring new staff in the area. Assist with analyzing current business processes and existing policies and make recommendations to drive continuous improvement and maximize resources in the graduation clearance area. Assist with maintaining standard procedures/documentation for degree clearance Percentage Of Time 5% Key Responsibility Customer Service/Special Projects Essential Tasks Assist with special projects. Provide customer service via frontline support and respond to emails via generic “registrars” email account during peak peri. Percentage Of Time 5% Key Responsibility Other duties as assigned Essential Tasks Prepare, conduct, and represent the University Registrar’s Office at campus events (e.g., SOAR , Commencement). Other duties as assigned. ADA Checklist ADA Checklist R for Rare (0-30%), O for Occasional (30-60%), F for Frequent (60-90%), C for Constant (90-100%). Physical Effort Work Environment Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate how you learned of the vacant position for which you are applying: UNCGjobsearch Website Greensboro News & Record Carolina Peacemaker Other Newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education Inside Higher Ed Other Professional Journal NCWorks.gov UNC System Job Board Other Online Job Board Personal Networking Other * If you selected \"Other\", please provide the name of the resource here. (Open Ended Question) * Are you eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment at the University of North Carolina in Greensboro? Yes No UNCG Human Resources UNC Greensboro 723 Kenilworth St. Greensboro, NC 27402-6170 Telephone 336.334.5009 Fax 336.334.5585 Back to top Copyright © 2025. UNC Greensboro. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
