    "https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35696": {
      "title": "Director of Enrollment Communications",
      "description": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities | Director of Enrollment Communications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Current UNCG Employee Log In UNC System Careers Director of Enrollment Communications Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Number 000348 Functional Title Director of Enrollment Communications Position Type Administration - Staff Position Eclass E2 - SAAO II 12 Month Leave Earning University Information Located in North Carolina’s third largest city, UNC Greensboro is among the most diverse, learner-centered public research universities in the state, with 18,000 students in eight colleges and schools pursuing more than 150 areas of undergraduate and over 200 areas of graduate study. UNCG continues to be recognized nationally for academic excellence, access, and affordability. UNCG is ranked No. 1 most affordable institution in North Carolina for net cost by the N.Y. Times and No. 1 in North Carolina for social mobility by The Wall Street Journal — helping first-generation and lower-income students find paths to prosperity. Designated an Innovation and Economic Prosperity University by the Association of Public and Land-grant Universities, UNCG is a community-engaged research institution with a portfolio of more than $67M in research and creative activity. The University’s 2,600 staff help create an annual economic impact for the Piedmont Triad region in excess of $1B. Primary Purpose of the Organizational Unit University Advancement elevates UNCG’s reputation, advances institutional strategy, and fosters community pride through integrated communications aligned with its public mission as a student-centered research university. The department develops and executes strategic communications and marketing initiatives that enhance visibility, engage key audiences, and convey the University’s distinctive value. Working across schools, colleges, and administrative units, University Communications manages media relations, marketing campaigns, content strategy, branding, digital engagement, sponsorships, and crisis communications. Position Summary The Director, Office of Enrollment Communications, will serve as the primary strategic leader for the University’s enrollment marketing efforts. The director will closely collaborate with leadership in the Division of Enrollment Management, The Graduate School, the Division of Student Success, University Communications, and various academic units to develop data-driven marketing strategies that increase enrollment (on-campus and online) and improve student experience. This individual is responsible for identifying and understanding marketing needs and leading the planning and executing of multiple, complex integrated campaigns that will drive University enrollment. Specific responsibilities include: Annual strategic planning for marketing campaigns (collateral/direct mail/advertising) to support undergraduate and graduate student recruitment (on-campus and online), admission communications, new student onboarding, Financial Aid, Registration, and other business processes for enrolled students. Website management for multiple entities including Enrollment, Admissions, Graduate School, and Spartan Central (Financial Aid, Registrar, and Cashiers Office). Administration and oversight of content creation for communication-related elements of Undergraduate Admissions and Graduate School CRM systems. This position will be supported by a team of digital and traditional marketing professionals, including strategic experts, project managers, and a small creative staff (copywriting/design). The director will lead the department staff to work with agility and knowledge, which requires a leader who possesses a breadth of marketing/communications experience and a willingness to roll up their sleeves and do project-level work at times. They should be as savvy at developing new strategies as they are at executing them. The ideal individual must have a well-rounded knowledge of integrated marketing communications disciplines and a track record of executing on strategic campaigns that exceed expectations while remaining on time and on budget. This individual must demonstrate a commitment to continual learning — for themselves and their staff members — to stay on top of industry trends. Expert leadership skills are required and should include presentation skills, budget management, reporting, consulting, supervision, and a track record of staff development. Some project management, copywriting, and basic graphic design skills will be required on occasion. Prior experience managing print projects, especially in a higher-ed setting, is ideal. Minimum Qualifications Candidates for this position must possess a Master’s Degree + at least 12 years professional marketing experience, or a Bachelor’s Degree + at least 15 years professional marketing experience. Experience must include: 8+ years in a strategic planning capacity, collaborating with a team to brainstorm and execute on complex, creative ideas that meet company goals. 5+ years supervisory experience. 3+ years in roles with budget accountability. 3+ years work experience in higher education. Additional minimum qualification requirements: Proven track record of success in developing and executing creative, data-driven marketing campaigns that deliver results. Proven ability to manage multiple projects across a variety of channels with fast-paced timelines. Excellent communication skills both oral and written and the ability to build strong and collaborative cross-functional relationships. Experience leading a team of writers, designers, project managers, digital marketers, external vendors, and project owners to deliver efficient output and results. Proven attention to detail and organizational skills. Willingness to work flexible and extended schedule including weekends and evenings on occasion for University events, filming, etc. Additional Required Certifications, Licensures, and Certificates Preferred Qualifications Extensive work experience in higher ed, specifically in roles supporting recruitment and enrollment marketing for large, public universities. Expertise in best practices and regulations around bulk mail, CAN - SPAM , GDPR , web privacy, and other regulatory guidelines. Copywriting and design capabilities (to include Adobe Creative Suite). Advertising/Marketing agency experience (either as a client or as an agency representative). Experience in any of the following areas: Print project management. Coordinating and directing photo/video shoots. Email/Text comm flow design. Knowledge of any of the following: Google Analytics Google AdWords WordPress Emma (or similar) email platform Slate/Technolutions Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Range $85,000 – $90,000 Org #-Department University Communications - 33901 Job Open Date 08/14/2026 For Best Consideration Date 08/30/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No FTE 1.000 Type of Appointment Permanent If time-limited, please specify end date for appointment. Number of Months per Year 12 FLSA Exempt Key Responsibilities ________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Percentage Of Time 30% Key Responsibility Enrollment Management Partnership & Advocacy Essential Tasks Serve as the primary marketing liaison to Enrollment Management leadership and key campus partners including Admissions, Financial Aid, the Registrar, Graduate School, Cashiers Office, and related units. Understand institutional enrollment goals and translate complex enrollment policies, processes, and priorities into actionable marketing initiatives and communication plans. Advise Enrollment Management leadership on marketing best practices and trends as they relate to key audiences. Represent and advocate for the needs, expectations, and perceptions of prospective students and families in institutional messaging, brand positioning, and marketing decision making. Provide expert input on university-wide messages and campaigns from an enrollment perspective. Represent and advocate for the needs, expectations, and perceptions of prospective students and families in institutional messaging, brand positioning, and marketing decision making. Provide expert input on university-wide messages and campaigns from an enrollment perspective. Percentage Of Time 30% Key Responsibility Enrollment Communications Marketing & Campaign Strategy Essential Tasks Directly develop and manage enrollment marketing campaigns, communication plans, messaging strategies, and recruitment initiatives. Lead audience segmentation, communication planning, and channel strategy for prospective and enrolled student populations. Collaborate with creative, web, advertising, content, and social media teams to coordinate campaign execution. Review and approve enrollment-focused marketing assets and communications to ensure accuracy, effectiveness, and alignment with institutional goals Percentage Of Time 15% Key Responsibility CRM Communications, Digital Engagement, & Marketing Operations Essential Tasks Provide strategic and operational oversight for enrollment communication systems, digital engagement tactics, and related marketing infrastructure. Oversee enrollment communication strategy across CRM , email, text messaging, portals, websites, and other student-facing communication channels. Partner with technical and operational staff to support communication workflows, automation, campaign deployment, and audience management. Lead communication calendar planning and coordination across enrollment-related departments. Identify opportunities to improve communication effectiveness through testing, optimization, process improvements, and emerging technologies. Percentage Of Time 15% Key Responsibility Team Leadership & Operational Management Essential Tasks Lead the enrollment communications team and manage resources, processes, and operations necessary to support enrollment marketing priorities. Supervise, mentor, and develop professional staff responsible for enrollment communication planning, CRM operations, and project execution. Establish operational priorities, workflows, service standards, and project management practices to support efficient execution. Manage enrollment-related marketing budgets, vendor relationships, contracts, and production resources. Foster a culture of accountability, collaboration, innovation, and continuous improvement. Percentage Of Time 10% Key Responsibility Performance Measurement & Insight Development Essential Tasks Ensure enrollment marketing decisions are informed by data, audience insights, and enrollment outcomes Monitor enrollment funnel trends, campaign performance, and marketing metrics to identify growth opportunities and improve effectiveness. Research emerging communication channels, technologies, and best practices and implement recommendations as appropriate. Serve as a campus resource and subject matter expert for student communications and enrollment marketing. ADA Checklist ADA Checklist R for Rare (0-30%), O for Occasional (30-60%), F for Frequent (60-90%), C for Constant (90-100%). Physical Effort Hand Movement-Repetitive Motions - F, Finger Dexterity - F, Reading - F, Writing - F, Hearing - F, Talking - F, Sitting - F, Standing - F, Walking - F Work Environment Inside - F Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate how you learned of the vacant position for which you are applying: UNCGjobsearch Website Greensboro News & Record Carolina Peacemaker Other Newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education Inside Higher Ed Other Professional Journal NCWorks.gov UNC System Job Board Other Online Job Board Personal Networking Other * If you selected \"Other\", please provide the name of the resource here. (Open Ended Question) * Are you eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment at the University of North Carolina in Greensboro? Yes No UNCG Human Resources UNC Greensboro 723 Kenilworth St. Greensboro, NC 27402-6170 Telephone 336.334.5009 Fax 336.334.5585 Back to top Copyright © 2025. UNC Greensboro. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35459": {
      "title": "Manager of Student Health Access",
      "description": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities | Manager of Student Health Access Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Current UNCG Employee Log In UNC System Careers Manager of Student Health Access Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Number 005275 Functional Title Manager of Student Health Access Position Type Staff Position Eclass EP - EHRA 12 mo leave earning University Information Located in North Carolina’s third largest city, UNC Greensboro is among the most diverse, learner-centered public research universities in the state, with 18,000 students in eight colleges and schools pursuing more than 150 areas of undergraduate and over 200 areas of graduate study. UNCG continues to be recognized nationally for academic excellence, access, and affordability. UNCG is ranked No. 1 most affordable institution in North Carolina for net cost by the N.Y. Times and No. 1 in North Carolina for social mobility by The Wall Street Journal — helping first-generation and lower-income students find paths to prosperity. Designated an Innovation and Economic Prosperity University by the Association of Public and Land-grant Universities, UNCG is a community-engaged research institution with a portfolio of more than $67M in research and creative activity. The University’s 2,600 staff help create an annual economic impact for the Piedmont Triad region in excess of $1B. Primary Purpose of the Organizational Unit The mission of Student Health Services is to provide collaborative health care designed to empower students to develop lifelong skills that enhance their physical, psychological and wellness status in an inclusive and affirming environment. Student Health Service. Provides student-centered, medical, counseling and health promotion services which are affordable and accessible. Utilizes a multidisciplinary and collaborative approach to wellness and health care. Provides an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of diversity. Promotes professional excellence, responsiveness and ethical practice. Is committed to the support of the educational, research and service missions of the University. Position Summary The Manager of Student Health Access provides leadership and oversight for student-facing administrative operations within Student Health Services. This position is responsible for healthcare access services, insurance administration, provider credentialing, revenue cycle support, health information oversight, STAT referral coordination, customer service operations, and administrative support functions. The manager serves as a primary resource for students, staff, providers, and external partners regarding healthcare access, insurance coverage, billing processes, medical records, and operational services while ensuring compliance with university policies, HIPAA regulations, accreditation standards, and healthcare industry best practices. The position supervises administrative support staff and develops processes that support efficient operations and a positive student experience. Minimum Qualifications Relevant bachelor’s degree and one year of experience related to the area of assignment. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Additional Required Certifications, Licensures, and Certificates Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Health Information Management or related discipline; or completion of an accredited Medical Record Technician program and two years of experience in Medical Record work. Experience in Health Information and electronic health records. Full knowledge regarding HIPAA . Experience in University/College Health. Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Range $54,500 – $60,000 Org #-Department Student Health Services - 44604 Job Open Date 07/20/2026 For Best Consideration Date 08/03/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes FTE 1.000 Type of Appointment Permanent If time-limited, please specify end date for appointment. Number of Months per Year 12 FLSA Exempt Key Responsibilities ________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Percentage Of Time 25% Key Responsibility Student Access & Support Services Essential Tasks Oversees front desk and student support operations. Ensures exceptional customer service for students, parents, faculty, staff, and visitors. Assists students with insurance questions, billing concerns, STAT referrals, and healthcare navigation. Serves as a resource regarding student accounts, insurance coverage, healthcare access, and SHS administrative processes. Coordinates communication between students, providers, Mental Health and Spartan Well-Being, Student Affairs, and external healthcare organizations. Supports SOAR and other student engagement initiatives. Develops and implements service standards that support a student-centered environment. Percentage Of Time 25% Key Responsibility Insurance Administration, Credentialing & Revenue Operations Essential Tasks Oversees provider credentialing and recredentialing activities with commercial and governmental insurance carriers. Serves as Office Administrator for Medicaid enrollment and credentialing. Maintains provider participation with BCBS , Cigna, MedCost, United Healthcare, CorVel, Zelis, and other payers. Manages payer portals and provider enrollment systems. Serves as secondary administrator for Waystar and insurance-related systems. Oversees ERA enrollment and electronic payment processes. Processes refunds and account adjustments related to healthcare services. Responds to insurance, billing, and student account inquiries. Collaborates with billing and accounts receivable functions. Assists with revenue cycle workflow development and process improvement. Percentage Of Time 20% Key Responsibility Health Information Administration & Compliance Essential Tasks Oversees management of health information contained within electronic health records and related systems. Ensures compliance with HIPAA , FERPA , university policies, and healthcare regulations regarding privacy, confidentiality, retention, release, and security of information. Maintains policies and procedures related to health information management. Conducts routine audits and quality assurance reviews of records and documentation. Coordinates responses to requests for medical information and documentation. Maintains administrative oversight of medical records processes. Provides guidance to clinical and administrative staff regarding records management and documentation requirements. Supports accreditation, licensing, compliance, and regulatory review activities. Ensures security of protected health information. Percentage Of Time 15% Key Responsibility Care Coordination & Operational Support Essential Tasks Coordinates STAT referrals and continuity of care activities. Supports emergency room transfers and follow-up processes. Coordinates emergency transportation services and after-hours support arrangements. Manages incident reporting processes and administrative follow-up. Collaborates with clinical staff to improve patient flow and operational efficiency. Participates in Medicat implementation and optimization efforts. Participates in provider meetings, leadership meetings, worker’s compensation meetings, fee committee activities, and operational planning initiatives. Develops workflows and procedures that improve efficiency and service delivery. Percentage Of Time 10% Key Responsibility Leadership, Supervision & Performance Management Essential Tasks Supervises Student Support Specialists, Administrative Support Specialists, and other assigned personnel. Develops work schedules and staffing plans to ensure operational coverage. Conducts recruitment, onboarding, training, coaching, and performance evaluations. Monitors employee performance and implements corrective action when necessary. Develops staff competencies related to customer service, insurance administration, health information management, and operational support. Promotes professional development opportunities for direct reports. Percentage Of Time 5% Key Responsibility Strategic Initiatives & Other Duties Essential Tasks Participates in departmental strategic planning initiatives. Supports implementation of new technologies and operational improvements. Assists with departmental projects and university initiatives. Serves on committees and workgroups as assigned. Performs other duties as assigned in support of Student Health Services and university objectives. ADA Checklist ADA Checklist R for Rare (0-30%), O for Occasional (30-60%), F for Frequent (60-90%), C for Constant (90-100%). Physical Effort Hand Movement-Repetitive Motions - F, Finger Dexterity - F, Reading - F, Writing - F, Hearing - F, Talking - F, Standing - F, Sitting - F, Walking - F, Lifting-0-30 lbs. - F, Bending - F, Squatting - F Work Environment Inside - C Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe your experience with providing customer service to a variety of customer types. (Open Ended Question) * What does excellent customer service mean to you? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have any supervisory experience? Yes No * Do you have prior experience managing direct reports? If yes, length of time?  If yes, how many individuals? (Open Ended Question) * Please indicate how you learned of the vacant position for which you are applying: UNCGjobsearch Website Greensboro News & Record Carolina Peacemaker Other Newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education Inside Higher Ed Other Professional Journal NCWorks.gov UNC System Job Board Other Online Job Board Personal Networking Other * If you selected \"Other\", please provide the name of the resource here. (Open Ended Question) * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment at UNCG? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment at the University of North Carolina in Greensboro? Yes No UNCG Human Resources UNC Greensboro 723 Kenilworth St. Greensboro, NC 27402-6170 Telephone 336.334.5009 Fax 336.334.5585 Back to top Copyright © 2025. UNC Greensboro. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
